TYPE=u64
GROUP=call
DOC=HOW MANY SECONDS A DWARF SLEEPS BEFORE ITS SESSION STARTS. A batch of dwarves called
SCHEMA=Seconds of random delay before a dwarf's session starts (0 disables; unset: 20).
DEFAULT<<'SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF'
    # HOW MANY SECONDS A DWARF SLEEPS BEFORE ITS SESSION STARTS. A batch of dwarves called
    # together picks a uniform random delay in 0..=this many seconds (dwarf's own
    # spira_config::admission::jitter) so they do not all hit the claim store, the worktree
    # root and the model API in the same instant. 20s is the default (sp-f4ig1); matches
    # dwarf/src/../spira-config/src/admission.rs's JITTER_DEFAULT, which this registry entry
    # exists to keep in sync with, not to override — change both together (sp-1cdgq).
    : "${SPIRA_CALL_JITTER:=20}"
SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF
